orkers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336107" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336107" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "the definition of a basis"] ["text" "the definition of matrix multiplication"] ["text" "the properties of determinants"] ["text" "the transitive property of equality"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336107" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "the transitive property of equality"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ states the independence of the columns of {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L3}$ by the {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first interpret line $\\text{L2}.$ Line $\\text{L2}$ states that the two columns of $Φ(t)$ are linearly independent, which is required of a fundamental matrix. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ states independence of the columns of $Φ(t).$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Recall that a square matrix is invertible when its determinant is nonzero. Since in $\\text{L3}$ we have that $det(Φ(t))\\ne 0$ for all $t,$ it follows that $Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t.$ Thus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ by the $\\text{properties of invertible matrices}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9108dced82c6cb3acf6ef30d87531244a88a01288772cefc5d4d3f20b5e123ab"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "A"] ["math" "{A}^{-1}"] ["math" "{Φ}^{-1}"] ["math" "Φ(t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Φ(t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "definition of a fundamental matrix"] ["text" "definition of matrix multiplication"] ["text" "properties of invertible matrices"] ["text" "substituting ${Φ}^{′}=A\\,Φ$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "definition of a fundamental matrix"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "definition of a fundamental matrix"] ["text" "definition of matrix multiplication"] ["text" "properties of invertible matrices"] ["text" "substituting ${Φ}^{′}=A\\,Φ$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-336093" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "properties of invertible matrices"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that $Φ(t)$ satisfies the matrix differential equation ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A\\,Φ(t)$ is given below.\n\n*Hint: $[a,\\,b]$ denotes a matrix whose columns are vectors $a$ and $b.$*\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let $Φ(t)=[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[{x}_{1}^{′}(t),\\,{x}_{2}^{′}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=[A{x}_{1}(t),\\,A{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=A[{x}_{1}(t),\\,{x}_{2}(t)]$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}(t)=AΦ(t)$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line $\\text{L4}$ and substitution from lines {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are linearly independent solutions of the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$ This means that each column satisfies the differential equation. In particular, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L2}$ follows from the fact that ${x}_{1}\\text{ is a solution of the system}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L4}$ and $\\text{L5}.$ By definition, the derivative of $Φ(t)$ is obtained by differentiating each column,\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}^{′}(t) & {x}_{2}^{′}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing ${x}_{1}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{1}(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ and ${x}_{2}^{′}(t)=A{x}_{2}(t)$ from $\\text{L3},$ we substitute each derivative into the matrix to get\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L5}$ follows from $\\text{L4}$ by substitution from $\\text{L2}\\text{ and }\\text{L3}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ We now factor the matrix $A$ on the left:\n\n$$\n{Φ}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ A{x}_{1}(t) & A{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}]=A[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}]=AΦ(t)\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{factoring out }A\\text{ on the left}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9108dced82c6cb3acf6ef30d87531244a88a01288772cefc5d4d3f20b5e123ab"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ is diagonalizable"] ["text" "${x}_{1}$ is a solution of the system"] ["text" "${x}_{1}$ is differentiable"] ["text" "$Φ(t)$ is invertible for all $t$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${x}_{1}$ is a solution of the system"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$"] ["text" "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$"] ["text" "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "adding $Φ(t)$ to both sides"] ["text" "differentiating again"] ["text" "factoring out $A$ on the left"] ["text" "transposing the matrix"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333719" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "factoring out $A$ on the left"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant $2\\times 2$ matrix. Let $Φ(t)$ be a fundamental matrix for this system. A derivation showing that every solution $x(t)$ can be written in the form $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c=[{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}]^{T}$ is given below.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ be the columns of $Φ(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of solutions\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)$ can be written as $x(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $Φ(t)\\,c={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t)$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(t)=Φ(t)\\,c$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by the {{field-3}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis of the solution space for our system. Thus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Once ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ form a basis, every solution $x(t)$ of the system can be expressed uniquely as a linear combination\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ by $\\text{the definition of a basis}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Since ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are the columns of $Φ(t),$ we can write\n\n$$\nΦ(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen by the definition of matrix multiplication,\n\n$$\nΦ(t)\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}\\,| & | \\\\ {x}_{1}(t) & {x}_{2}(t) \\\\ \\,| & |\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}]={c}_{1}{x}_{1}(t)+{c}_{2}{x}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{definition of matrix multiplication}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9108dced82c6cb3acf6ef30d87531244a88a01288772cefc5d4d3f20b5e123ab"} {"question" "q-333723" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/d