"ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333723" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333723" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "definition of a fundamental matrix"] ["text" "definition of matrix multiplication"] ["text" "fact that $Φ$ is nonsingular"] ["text" "properties of invertible matrices"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333723" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "definition of matrix multiplication"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 5{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ -5{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\text{i}t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-5\\text{i}t,\n$$\n\nwhich are complex conjugates. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r((5\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(5\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(5\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0}+5\\text{i}{\\alpha }_{1}t & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}=\\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9108dced82c6cb3acf6ef30d87531244a88a01288772cefc5d4d3f20b5e123ab"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(5t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sin(5t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\sin(5t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-334382" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\cos(5t)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear ODEs ${x}^{′}=Ax$ with the matrix $A$ shown above. Compute the **standard** fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ for this system.\n\n| ${Φ}_{0}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$ |  | ${e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | ${e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}$ |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $A$ is a constant $n\\times n$ matrix and $x(t)$ is an $n\\times 1$ column vector. The standard fundamental matrix of the linear system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ denoted ${Φ}_{0}(t),$ is the unique matrix solution of the initial value problem \n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{n}$ is the identity matrix. \n\nFurthermore, it can be shown that ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}.$\n\nWe have a square matrix of dimension $n=2.$ Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{At} & ={\\alpha }_{1}At+{\\alpha }_{0}I \\\\  & ={\\alpha }_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]t+{\\alpha }_{0}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & 2{\\alpha }_{1}t \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & {\\alpha }_{0}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ are constants to be determined.\n\nConsider the polynomial $r(\\lambda )={\\alpha }_{1}\\lambda +{\\alpha }_{0}.$ The eigenvalues of $At$ are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-2t,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2t,\n$$\n\nboth of multiplicity one. Thus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}r(-2t)={e}^{-2t} \\\\ r(2t)={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,{\\begin{aligned}-2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t} \\\\ 2t{\\alpha }_{1}+{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the system for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n- Subtraction the second equation from the first one, we get\n\n$$\n-4t{\\alpha }_{1}={e}^{-2t}-{e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{1}=-\\frac{1}{4t}({e}^{-2t}-{e}^{2t}).\n$$\n\n- Adding the first and the second equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{\\alpha }_{0}={e}^{-2t}+{e}^{2t}\\,⇒\\,{\\alpha }_{0}=\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-2t}+{e}^{2t}).\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{0} & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{-2t}+{e}^{2t}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}) \\\\ 2{\\alpha }_{1}t & =2\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{4t}({e}^{-4t}-{e}^{4t}))t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}-{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{2t}+{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9108dced82c6cb3acf6ef30d87531244a88a01288772cefc5d4d3f20b5e123ab"} {"question" "q-333715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070844/state.json" "file_sha256" "cae41375d9854e678f9299c1588c33616a29253eb6ae6b40b8702e80bd1963e0"} {"question" "q-333715" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^{2t}-e^{-2t}"] "category" 